      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W4299" name="W4299. Appliance &amp; White-Goods Installation, Hookup &amp; Commissioning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Item install-required flag (W4292); delivery handoff (W4298)
Frequency: Per install-tagged bulky order
Volume: Install-tagged orders (split-AC, water heater, washing machine, cooker, rangehood, dishwasher)
Owner: Licensed Installer / Bulky-Delivery Service Ops / Installation Services (VS-12)
Participants: Installer (W4293), Crew, Customer Service (VS-13), Quality (VS-31), HSE (VS-24)
Source: workflow W4299 — Appliance &amp; White-Goods Installation, Hookup &amp; Commissioning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4299_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4299_Lane1" name="Installer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4299_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4299_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4299_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4299_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4299_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4299_Start3" name="Item install-required flag (W4292); delivery handoff (W4298)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4299_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4299_Task4" name="Installer perform the hookup/commissioning per category SOP — electrical…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Installer perform the hookup/commissioning per category SOP — electrical (cooker/washer), plumbing (washer/dishwasher/water heater), refrigerant split-AC (vacuum/charge/leak-test per RA 8749 Clean Air Act), gas (cooker — gas-safe), and venting (rangehood/dryer)
Responsible (R): Installer
Accountable (A): Crew Lead / Service Mgr
Duration: Per install</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4299_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4299_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4299_Task5" name="Installer test function, leak/safety-check (gas leak, refrigerant leak…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Installer test function, leak/safety-check (gas leak, refrigerant leak, electrical, level/stability), brief the customer on operation/maintenance, and hand over manuals/warranty card
Responsible (R): Installer
Accountable (A): Service Mgr
Duration: Per install</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4299_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4299_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4299_Task6" name="Installer register the install/warranty (VS-53), capture install evidence…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Installer register the install/warranty (VS-53), capture install evidence (photos, serial, completion), and post the install-fee/service revenue (VS-16/VS-17)
Responsible (R): Installer / Service Ops
Accountable (A): Service Mgr
Duration: Per install</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4299_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4299_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4299_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4299_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4299_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-660 (ensure controlled execution — Delivery Execution, Installation &amp; In-Home Service Operations (PA-143.2).) | - CTL-660: installer licensed (W4293); leak/safety test documented; warranty registered (VS-53); install evidence captured
Owner: Licensed Installer / Bulky-Delivery Service Ops / Installation Services (VS-12)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
