    <bpmn:process id="W_W4300" name="W4300. Installation Quality, Damage/Defect-on-Delivery &amp; Field Resolution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Damage found at delivery; defect-on-arrival; install-quality issue
Frequency: Per exception (benchmark 1–3% of bulky deliveries)
Volume: ~1–3% of bulky stops → damage/defect exceptions
Owner: Bulky-Delivery Service Ops / Quality (VS-31) / Damage Claims (VS-90)
Participants: Crew/Installer, Customer Service (VS-13), Quality (VS-31), Vendor (VS-03), Claims (VS-90), LP (VS-23)
Source: workflow W4300 — Installation Quality, Damage/Defect-on-Delivery &amp; Field Resolution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4300_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4300_Lane1" name="Crew">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4300_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4300_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4300_Lane2" name="Service Ops">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4300_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4300_Lane3" name="Claims">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4300_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4300_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4300_Start5" name="Damage found at delivery; defect-on-arrival; install-quality issue">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4300_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4300_Task6" name="Crew/Installer detect and document damage/defect at the point of…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Crew/Installer detect and document damage/defect at the point of delivery/install (photo, serial, nature), offer the customer options (accept-as-is with concession, refuse, swap), and capture the decision on e-POD
Responsible (R): Crew / Installer
Accountable (A): Crew Lead / Service Mgr
Duration: Per exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4300_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4300_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4300_Task7" name="Service Ops/Quality triage — transit damage (vs VS-06/VS-56 carrier)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Service Ops/Quality triage — transit damage (vs VS-06/VS-56 carrier), manufacturing defect (vs VS-31/VS-03 vendor DOA), or install error — and trigger recovery: redelivery (W4302), vendor RMA (VS-90/VS-31), or field repair
Responsible (R): Service Ops / Quality
Accountable (A): Service Mgr
Duration: Per exception</bpmn:documentation>
